$ moolah init --base EUR --no-backup-key
Book "main" is ready in $TMP/data/books/main.db (base currency EUR).
Next: add your accounts, for example:
  moolah account add Checking --kind bank --currency EUR --opening 1000
  moolah category list

$ moolah account add checking --kind bank --currency EUR
Added account checking (EUR).

$ moolah import $TMP/statement.csv --account checking
error: no import profile matches this file. Create one from it with: moolah profile create $TMP/statement.csv
or choose a profile with --profile
[exit 1]

$ moolah profile create $TMP/statement.csv
error: profile create asks questions, so it needs a terminal. Without one, write the profile by hand and save it with: moolah profile add <file.toml>
[exit 1]

$ moolah profile create $TMP/statement.csv    # answers: 1 | 1 |  |  |  | mybank | 5 | q
File: CSV, 2 transaction rows.
Column names are in line 2; the lines above it are skipped.
The dates in "Booking date" (for example 03/10/2026) can be read in more than one way.
   1  dd/mm/yyyy → 3 October 2026
   2  mm/dd/yyyy → 10 March 2026
Which is right? [1]: Each row has an amount in either "Debit" or "Credit".
   1  "Debit" (for example "123,40")
   2  "Credit" (for example "3.500,00")
Which column is money out (debit)? [1]: Payee (description): "Text" (for example "SUPERMARKET", "SALARY ACME"). Right? [Y/n]: Is "Reference" (for example "100234", "100235") the bank's reference number? moolah then uses it to recognize rows imported before. [Y/n]: Line 5, after the transactions, has "Total" (a total?). Stop reading there? [Y/n]: Profile name (for example the bank's name) [statement]: 
   1  date         "Booking date", dd/mm/yyyy
   2  amount       debit "Debit" (money out), credit "Credit" (money in)
   3  currency     the account's currency
   4  foreign      none
   5  payee        "Text"
   6  note         none
   7  reference    "Reference"
   8  charge date  none
   9  installments none
  10  skip rows    none
  11  read until   the row with "Total"
  12  name         mybank
      Not used: "Balance"

The file as it would be imported (2 rows):
  line 3    2026-10-03  SUPERMARKET                            -123.4
  line 4    2026-10-04  SALARY ACME                              3500

[s]ave, [1-12] change a line, [e]dit the profile text, [q]uit [s]:    1  "Text" (for example "SUPERMARKET", "SALARY ACME")
Which column is the payee (description)? [1]: Type a number from 1 to 1.
Which column is the payee (description)? [1]: error: no answer (input ended)
[exit 1]

